WEBVTT

00:12.130 --> 00:19.990
Gouyokuou...

00:22.150 --> 00:23.500
Gekka...

00:23.710 --> 00:27.540
He waited for a thousand years,
so another day or two won't mean a thing.

00:30.610 --> 00:33.420
I'm waiting for you, Gekka.

01:51.840 --> 01:55.870
This story is a diary of a family that fought against the expected doom.

01:55.870 --> 02:02.160
The miracle of eight people without blood relation becoming a family has been animated without missing any details!

02:29.520 --> 02:32.000
Enter the authentication code.

02:32.000 --> 02:33.280
Let's see...

02:33.670 --> 02:35.130
It's Kyouka-sama!

02:39.820 --> 02:42.470
Father, her voice got authenticated.

02:46.310 --> 02:48.700
Dad! Mom! And Hyouka, too!

02:48.700 --> 02:49.900
You were all okay!

02:49.900 --> 02:50.730
Where are the others?

02:50.730 --> 02:52.480
They're all safe.

02:52.480 --> 02:53.550
Oh, thank goodness.

02:53.550 --> 02:54.610
Hey, where's Gekka-chan?

02:54.610 --> 02:57.670
Don't worry. She'll wiggle back in a bit.

02:57.670 --> 03:00.940
This shelter manager has been really kind to us.

03:00.940 --> 03:01.950
Manager?

03:01.950 --> 03:05.570
She's a really strange one! Not like I can speak of others.

03:05.570 --> 03:07.240
Her entire body has a design on it.

03:07.240 --> 03:08.660
Moo!

03:08.660 --> 03:09.750
And she wears a mask?

03:09.750 --> 03:10.830
Wild!

03:11.210 --> 03:12.710
And wears... what? A loincloth?

03:12.710 --> 03:13.840
Meow!

03:15.580 --> 03:17.980
Are we to expect another strange person?

03:18.920 --> 03:21.520
Mother, where are you going?

03:21.520 --> 03:22.300
We're leaving.

03:23.580 --> 03:27.780
Since I've already eradicated the vicious monsters that were walking around.

03:27.780 --> 03:31.140
So there's no need for us to stay in a cramped shelter like this.

03:27.780 --> 03:29.140
But you...

03:31.140 --> 03:32.650
Bakka Kyoukya!

03:32.650 --> 03:35.110
I missed you so much!

03:35.900 --> 03:37.650
Don't be so familiar with me!

03:37.650 --> 03:40.030
Bakka Kyoukya...

03:40.450 --> 03:42.440
You shouldn't punch others suddenly like that!

03:41.090 --> 03:43.660
I knew it was you, Kyupi Do.

03:42.440 --> 03:43.290
Are you all right?

03:42.440 --> 03:43.660
Did she call her Baka Kyouka?

03:43.960 --> 03:45.530
She called Kitty stupid!

03:45.530 --> 03:48.960
Not Baka Kyouka! She called me Bakka Kyoukya!

03:48.960 --> 03:50.600
Bakka Kyoukya?

03:50.600 --> 03:54.960
Bakka means "my master", and it's to honor me.

03:54.960 --> 04:01.320
And Kyoukya is my, Kyouka-sama's, name back in my home, the underground empire, Shangri-La!

04:02.920 --> 04:06.280
This punch. This pain. She indeed is Bakka Kyoukya!

04:06.280 --> 04:08.060
This must be the Enka-sama's guidance!

04:08.060 --> 04:09.600
I'm so glad to see you're safe!

04:10.180 --> 04:11.350
Stop it, Kyouka!

04:11.350 --> 04:12.690
Bakka Kyoukya!

04:12.690 --> 04:14.420
If you jump on me...

04:14.420 --> 04:15.400
Bakka Kyoukya!

04:15.400 --> 04:16.590
...with your brute strength,

04:16.590 --> 04:17.770
Bakka Kyoukya!

04:17.770 --> 04:20.230
It really hurts!!!

04:28.110 --> 04:33.590
By losing your presence, the underground empire's public order has fallen to new depths.

04:33.590 --> 04:36.840
If we hadn't agreed on signing the mutual nonaggression treaty with the Great Japanese Empire,

04:36.840 --> 04:40.920
there'd have been a chance that we wouldn't
have been able to maintain our independence.

04:40.920 --> 04:42.490
Mutual nonaggression treaty?

04:42.490 --> 04:44.720
Bakka Kyoukya!

04:44.720 --> 04:48.810
The Great Japanese Empire will not invade the underground empire!

04:48.810 --> 04:54.840
But instead, when the Great Japanese Empire is in jeopardy, the citizens of the underground empire will help!

04:54.840 --> 04:55.850
Is the treaty.

04:55.850 --> 04:59.080
So that's why you're here as the shelter manager.

04:59.080 --> 05:02.260
It was a coincidence that we meet again!

05:02.260 --> 05:05.150
People may call that a miracle.

05:05.630 --> 05:10.390
Kyouka. You might have some catching up to do with her, so should we leave you two alone?

05:10.390 --> 05:11.870
Who are you?

05:11.870 --> 05:14.970
You're acting very familiar with Bakka Kyoukya.

05:14.970 --> 05:17.030
Should I dispose of him?

05:18.180 --> 05:22.490
Hey Kyupi. He is my husband.

05:22.490 --> 05:23.320
Husband?

05:23.320 --> 05:28.680
And I am his wife and the mother of the children you see here.

05:31.390 --> 05:32.200
Wife?

05:32.520 --> 05:33.560
Husband?

05:33.940 --> 05:36.750
So pass the word along to the others.

05:36.750 --> 05:39.480
"Kyouka-sama has no intention of going back to the underground empire."

05:39.480 --> 05:43.050
"Forget about me and live well."

05:46.640 --> 05:48.400
S-Stop it, you!

05:46.840 --> 05:49.990
Come back to us, Bakka Kyoukya!

05:48.400 --> 05:49.990
You mustn't resort to violence!

05:50.510 --> 05:53.080
Goddamn, Great Japanese Empire!

05:53.080 --> 05:55.160
This is so frustrating! They're so arrogant!

05:53.750 --> 05:55.160
Stop it, Kyupi!

05:57.160 --> 06:02.320
Kyouka-sama lived for twenty years being praised as the incarnation of Enka. As the God.

06:02.690 --> 06:05.420
I never questioned if I wasn't.

06:06.590 --> 06:12.350
I lived in a world where everyone would call black, white, if Kyouka-sama said that it was white.

06:12.890 --> 06:16.740
But, in that world, I never felt any warmth.

06:16.740 --> 06:21.860
Everyone around me would praise me
but would never see me as an individual.

06:22.330 --> 06:25.070
"Save us, Kyoukya-sama." "Oh, how grateful."

06:25.070 --> 06:26.240
That's what I heard constantly.

06:26.240 --> 06:28.360
I wanted to be saved, too.

06:28.360 --> 06:30.720
God wants to be loved, too.

06:30.720 --> 06:33.880
While I was in Heaven, I experienced Hell.

06:32.480 --> 06:33.630
Kyouka...

06:34.370 --> 06:38.630
I wasn't tricked into marrying Ouka!

06:38.630 --> 06:43.170
I don't know if you will understand,
but Kyouka-sama's having a very fulfilled life.

06:44.670 --> 06:46.760
If you didn't like the treatment down there, then we'll fix it!

06:46.760 --> 06:49.360
But why?! Why does it have to be you, Bakka Kyoukya?!

06:49.360 --> 06:52.150
Do you have to be the one playing the mother and wife role?!

06:52.150 --> 06:53.810
Give Bakka Kyoukya back to us!

06:52.410 --> 06:53.810
Come on now...

06:53.810 --> 06:55.530
Give her back to us.

06:57.640 --> 07:04.260
We might not know much of our Mother who we have been living with for so long.

07:04.700 --> 07:11.310
I bet Mother lived in Shangri-La as her heart desired to, just like now.

07:11.610 --> 07:15.130
And just like now, she must have been relied on by everyone.

07:16.990 --> 07:22.070
Mother must have been an important person in the underground empire, too.

07:22.070 --> 07:24.640
Mom wouldn't leave, would she?

07:24.640 --> 07:25.950
It'll be all right.

07:32.440 --> 07:34.220
So this is where you were.

07:37.220 --> 07:38.890
Everyone is worried about you.

07:39.260 --> 07:40.220
Let's go back.

07:40.220 --> 07:42.060
Kyouka-sama won't go anywhere!

07:43.740 --> 07:44.360
Kyouka?

07:44.360 --> 07:49.590
Ouka. I'm scared that I'll be separated from everyone forever if I leave their side.

07:50.490 --> 07:55.950
Since it's a family made by jumbling people together, it'll be easy to break it if it's tried.

07:55.950 --> 07:59.280
For a jumbled-together family, I think we're doing pretty well.

07:59.580 --> 08:03.000
You don't even know what family is!
Don't talk like you know it!

08:03.910 --> 08:04.900
You're right.

08:06.250 --> 08:07.950
I didn't have a home.

08:08.780 --> 08:10.610
Nor do I have memories of when I was little.

08:10.610 --> 08:12.640
I lost my parents, too.

08:18.630 --> 08:22.190
But now, I have a family that accepts me and loves me.

08:22.870 --> 08:29.400
I can't remember my parents' faces, but I'm now grateful to them for giving birth to me in this world.

08:47.130 --> 08:49.280
Gouyokuou...

08:50.060 --> 08:51.690
Gouyokuou...

08:52.990 --> 08:57.140
I'm very sorry about earlier. I panicked from the sudden joy.

08:57.140 --> 09:01.950
The family of Bakka Kyoukya is family to us, the underground empire, too.

09:01.950 --> 09:07.940
So first, although it's a tight place, allow me to give you my welcome!

09:08.390 --> 09:11.480
Whole roasted ubakutta and deep fried dorokujya!

09:11.480 --> 09:13.330
Nanikusotta stew, too?

09:13.330 --> 09:16.220
They're all my favorite foods!

09:17.110 --> 09:20.530
Both the appearances and the names are sketchy.

09:20.530 --> 09:22.660
But it tastes good.

09:22.660 --> 09:23.410
It's delicious.

09:23.410 --> 09:25.080
I simply can't take it!

09:25.080 --> 09:26.580
It looks good for my skin!

09:26.580 --> 09:31.590
I! Kyupi Do! Shall dance to entertain this moment!

09:31.590 --> 09:34.110
Yeah! Go go Kyupi!

09:34.110 --> 09:35.420
Bakka Kyoukya!

09:36.340 --> 09:38.320
Men to the right and left.

09:38.320 --> 09:40.330
Have you had enough to eat for starters?

09:40.330 --> 09:43.630
Play those instruments as you like.

09:43.630 --> 09:44.450
Go go!

09:44.450 --> 09:47.310
Forget skill. Mistakes are the brilliance in this.

09:47.310 --> 09:49.860
Hit them as your fingers please.

09:49.860 --> 09:50.690
Play away.

09:50.690 --> 09:51.890
PLACEHOLDER

09:50.690 --> 09:52.440
Ready for this?

09:51.890 --> 09:56.340
Everyone please. Play the melody in your heart.

09:56.340 --> 09:59.430
Beat the rhythm that comes to mind.

10:09.930 --> 10:11.650
So what's next?

10:15.730 --> 10:19.250
I'm having a taste of your home now.

10:19.830 --> 10:24.360
Food and clothes are different from those of the Great Japanese Empire,

10:24.360 --> 10:28.290
but they live as a family, get distressed, and laugh just like we do.

10:28.870 --> 10:30.810
I was thinking how nice that is.

10:31.950 --> 10:33.670
You are different from others.

10:33.670 --> 10:35.520
We come from different worlds.

10:35.840 --> 10:40.840
That occasionally becomes the cause of fights, but because we're different, it's fun.

10:41.230 --> 10:44.210
We're different, but we share the same time.

10:44.210 --> 10:47.580
We may not speak the same language, but there's a connection somewhere.

10:47.580 --> 10:49.670
All right, Kyouka-sama's dancing, too!

10:50.290 --> 10:52.290
A long, long, long, long, long time ago.

10:52.290 --> 10:54.340
A star came falling from the sky.

10:54.340 --> 10:56.300
Between the land and the land,

10:56.300 --> 10:58.110
opened a hole.

10:59.160 --> 11:01.790
Right where the hole opened...

11:01.790 --> 11:03.670
Right where it opened?

11:05.370 --> 11:13.680
Oh, the great Enka-sama. He bore a child there, led the ancestors, and gave the key to them.

11:11.810 --> 11:15.070
Kyupi! Show everyone more of your tricks!

11:15.070 --> 11:17.320
Yes, Bakka Kyoukya!

11:24.410 --> 11:25.740
Here's another trick!

11:25.740 --> 11:26.700
Crap!

11:35.000 --> 11:36.550
Here's another trick!

11:36.550 --> 11:37.420
Crap!

11:41.260 --> 11:42.020
Damn.

11:42.020 --> 11:43.050
What do you think you're doing?!

11:44.640 --> 11:46.930
That didn't look like a slip of the hand.

11:46.930 --> 11:48.560
You aimed for Father, didn't you?

11:49.230 --> 11:51.490
A human would die if they get stabbed by this.

11:49.230 --> 11:50.830
Get off, Teika!

11:51.490 --> 11:53.060
Stop it, Kyouka.

11:53.610 --> 11:56.430
I can understand how Kyupi-san would hate me.

11:56.430 --> 12:00.900
What are you saying?! Why didn't you get out of the way like always?!

12:00.900 --> 12:04.330
If it wasn't for Hyouka, you could have been dead!

12:03.750 --> 12:04.950
Kyouka...

12:04.950 --> 12:07.160
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

12:07.950 --> 12:09.540
Oasis-san.

12:11.460 --> 12:14.440
You didn't go back to space?

12:14.440 --> 12:16.570
Don't send me back without actually seeing me go.

12:16.570 --> 12:20.010
I still haven't figured out the mystery of what love is.

12:20.010 --> 12:21.960
But why are you here?

12:21.960 --> 12:23.380
Well...

12:23.380 --> 12:26.650
Wha... Whatever, who cares about me.

12:26.650 --> 12:29.650
Anyway, she isn't the one that tried to kill Ouka.

12:29.650 --> 12:30.790
There's someone else.

12:30.790 --> 12:32.790
That can't be possible.

12:32.790 --> 12:34.870
We all saw what happened with our own eyes.

12:34.870 --> 12:36.900
Yeah! It would have skewered him!

12:36.900 --> 12:38.620
She even aimed for his eyes!

12:38.620 --> 12:41.450
Yes, it was her that threw the sword,

12:41.450 --> 12:44.910
but there was a being that took control of her and made her throw the sword.

12:44.910 --> 12:46.780
I'll be mad if you lie.

12:46.780 --> 12:49.290
I didn't sense any signals that would have allowed that.

12:49.990 --> 12:51.390
I said wait.

12:51.390 --> 12:54.670
Even if you couldn't sense it, it is in her!

13:05.300 --> 13:06.840
See? Water's out.

13:06.840 --> 13:08.180
Who are you?!

13:08.180 --> 13:10.700
Where did you enter Kyupi's body from?!

13:11.420 --> 13:13.310
Through food and drink?

13:13.920 --> 13:15.350
I already ate them!

13:15.860 --> 13:18.600
Or maybe I snuck in while she was asleep.

13:19.090 --> 13:22.890
To be able to discern I was there. You must be Water, too.

13:22.890 --> 13:24.280
Why did you interrupt me?

13:24.840 --> 13:28.440
I'm the one asking the questions. Why are you doing this?

13:28.440 --> 13:34.750
I'm just looking for our God who's disguised as a human and living with them.

13:34.750 --> 13:36.610
God? You mean Kitty?

13:36.610 --> 13:39.420
I would never be a God of stupid creatures like them!

13:39.420 --> 13:41.340
I'm not too sure about that.

13:41.340 --> 13:43.540
Maybe I'll parasite on you and see what happens.

13:43.920 --> 13:46.470
After all, she wasn't our God, either.

13:48.790 --> 13:50.060
But let me tell you.

13:50.060 --> 13:53.770
It is my fault, yet not my fault for attacking that man.

13:53.770 --> 13:56.310
That's too complicated! Simplify it!

13:56.970 --> 14:06.000
Simply her wish of wanting to kill him and not wanting to lose you grew.

14:06.000 --> 14:10.700
Seems like whenever I parasite on others,
side-effects like that occur.

14:10.700 --> 14:12.650
That's really dangerous.

14:12.650 --> 14:15.200
I see. You must be the Princess.

14:15.580 --> 14:19.690
You were influenced by those on this planet, and you now stand in my way?

14:19.690 --> 14:23.510
But you're just a drop that was detached from me.

14:23.510 --> 14:27.380
No! I am an individual being named Oasis!

14:27.970 --> 14:31.750
I can feel the emotions you all can't!

14:32.890 --> 14:36.450
I don't know what that emotion is, but I am me!

14:38.900 --> 14:40.730
What was that about?

14:44.400 --> 14:47.310
How long do you intend to be sleeping? Get up!

14:44.900 --> 14:46.980
Yes... That feels good...

14:47.740 --> 14:51.960
Yes! Bakka Kyoukya! How could I have fallen asleep in the middle of a party!

14:51.960 --> 14:54.990
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

14:52.760 --> 14:54.990
You don't remember anything?

14:54.990 --> 14:58.830
I was having a dream I can't possibly describe to you.

15:00.670 --> 15:05.010
Give it back to me! It's not a kid's toy!

15:03.560 --> 15:04.710
Oh, here.

15:06.570 --> 15:09.670
I see. This is getting interesting.

15:11.750 --> 15:13.210
Gouyokuou...

15:14.100 --> 15:15.330
Gouyokuou...

15:16.040 --> 15:17.350
Gouyokuou...

15:28.880 --> 15:32.450
You were searching for me, right?

15:37.700 --> 15:42.460
You are having fun with others due to the stress of not being able to find me, right?

15:47.010 --> 15:48.780
I'm right here.

15:48.780 --> 15:50.630
I will neither hide nor run.

15:51.180 --> 15:53.540
What do you all wish for?

15:53.540 --> 15:57.270
What did you come here, following Gouyokuou, for?

15:58.140 --> 15:59.760
What for, you ask?

15:59.760 --> 16:02.650
Ask yourself why and think!

16:03.750 --> 16:05.240
Haven't got a clue.

16:05.600 --> 16:09.140
You're the God that abandoned us for a thousand years!

16:10.030 --> 16:12.530
Even calling you God irritates me!

16:16.470 --> 16:19.540
Our planet Ocean.

16:20.540 --> 16:24.070
The first intelligent species born from the Water of Life.

16:24.600 --> 16:31.110
You were lonely, being alone in the world, so you tore yourself apart and scattered your body, creating us.

16:38.680 --> 16:42.620
But one thousand years ago, when Gouyokuou came,

16:42.620 --> 16:46.570
you fled, leaving us behind,
without even trying to fight against him!

16:49.290 --> 16:53.800
Gouyokuou remained and claimed to become God's replacement.

16:53.800 --> 16:58.870
And a thousand years later, he said he'd go look for you and left Ocean.

16:59.520 --> 17:02.280
You plan on coming back now, acting like the ruler?

17:02.280 --> 17:03.570
I won't let you!

17:03.570 --> 17:05.200
The Ocean belongs to us!

17:05.200 --> 17:07.390
So you're here to kill me?

17:07.390 --> 17:10.150
That is why you followed Gouyokuou?

17:10.150 --> 17:12.380
Is that what you want to achieve?

17:13.870 --> 17:19.010
With you and Gouyokuou gone,
there won't be anyone terrorizing my Ocean.

17:19.010 --> 17:20.970
I will become the new God!

17:24.720 --> 17:25.900
Are you making a fool of me?

17:25.900 --> 17:28.530
Sorry, I said too much.

17:28.530 --> 17:29.700
But still...

17:31.250 --> 17:33.820
Have you lost your wits from the fear of death?

17:33.820 --> 17:36.460
I don't mind my death too much.

17:36.460 --> 17:38.910
But haven't you forgotten about something?

17:38.910 --> 17:40.260
What are you talking about?

17:40.260 --> 17:42.910
You and I are one.

17:42.910 --> 17:46.990
You were made from me to begin with.

17:46.990 --> 17:51.490
That is why we came here to be freed from your constraints...

17:55.220 --> 17:57.410
Do you finally realize?

17:57.410 --> 18:00.720
Kill me, and you'll die, too.

18:05.480 --> 18:09.690
S-S-S-S-S-S-So, if I killed you, I'll die, too?

18:09.690 --> 18:12.020
That's exactly what I just said.

18:12.020 --> 18:15.260
I can't lay a finger on you?!

18:15.260 --> 18:16.800
Looks like it...

18:20.610 --> 18:22.370
You fool.

18:23.230 --> 18:28.620
So the Water that came along with Gouyokuou is a big pain in the butt, eh?

18:28.620 --> 18:32.710
In a nutshell, yes, but you simplify things too much.

18:32.710 --> 18:35.860
Those who want to talk complicated stuff complicatedly are...

18:35.860 --> 18:37.760
...either trying to hide how stupid they are,...

18:37.760 --> 18:41.150
...or don't have a good understanding themselves.

18:41.150 --> 18:45.640
And those who talk about simple stuff complicatedly are stupid.

18:45.640 --> 18:49.510
But if the Water parasites on one of the Midarezaki, that's when the real trouble begins.

18:50.280 --> 18:57.150
Gouyokuou means no harm to humans, but the Child of Enka is a potential threat to humanity, right?

18:57.150 --> 19:02.460
It looks like the Operation Cozy Family is working favorably and they're getting along well,

19:02.460 --> 19:05.700
but we don't know what'll happen if the Water parasites on one of them.

19:06.920 --> 19:08.750
Strawberry-flavored chocolate?

19:08.750 --> 19:10.160
What do we do?

19:10.160 --> 19:11.380
What should we do with this?

19:11.380 --> 19:13.320
Not about the chocolate!

19:13.320 --> 19:15.000
Let's see...

19:15.000 --> 19:18.420
How about we start by separating the family?

19:18.420 --> 19:22.820
You mean you're calling Operation Cozy Family off for a moment?

19:22.820 --> 19:25.040
I don't think that's-

19:25.040 --> 19:26.270
Why not?

19:26.270 --> 19:31.760
If you do that, who will defeat the Gouyokuou?

19:31.760 --> 19:35.320
Isn't that why you were testing them and such until now?

19:35.320 --> 19:39.410
But Gouyokuou's being obedient right now,
so it might be our chance.

19:39.410 --> 19:42.280
We'll kill him with this missile.

19:43.970 --> 19:45.030
I don't like that.

19:45.030 --> 19:46.330
Million-sama!

19:46.930 --> 19:48.270
The missile button!

19:48.270 --> 19:49.210
I pressed it.

19:49.610 --> 19:53.330
Operation Cozy Family must continue.

19:55.070 --> 19:57.020
But, Million-sama!

19:57.020 --> 19:58.550
Did I just hear the word "but"?

19:59.230 --> 20:02.060
What's that? You're stating your opinion to me, Raichou-chan?

20:03.150 --> 20:07.260
I'm saying that separating the family is a bad idea.

20:07.260 --> 20:08.860
Families must always be together.

20:08.860 --> 20:11.090
For such a simple reason?

20:11.090 --> 20:13.480
Raichou-sama, you haven't forgotten, have you?

20:14.060 --> 20:19.580
Wakarazunomiya Million-sama is the heir of the world's greatest conglomerate, Wakarazunomiya.

20:20.070 --> 20:27.080
You received sanction thanks to her authority and
financial power, and made it up to being the Head here.

20:27.080 --> 20:29.160
Thanks for the reminder, Spider.

20:29.160 --> 20:32.600
Yeah, you are Million-sama's direct subordinate.

20:32.600 --> 20:36.850
If Million-sama wants to do away with me, then you will do so.

20:36.850 --> 20:39.590
Even so, Million-sama. I will say this.

20:39.590 --> 20:45.950
If Operation Cozy Family continues,
that family may face an unwanted ending!

20:45.930 --> 20:50.270
Aren't there important people to you in there, too?!

20:50.270 --> 20:51.950
How boring.

20:53.310 --> 20:57.050
I was looking forward to a fun chat with you today...

20:57.380 --> 20:59.500
So let's stop talking.

20:59.500 --> 21:01.460
Instead, show me a belly dance.

21:01.460 --> 21:01.950
What?

21:01.950 --> 21:06.120
You know. The one where you draw a face on the belly and make it look like it's smiling or crying.

21:06.120 --> 21:07.000
I'll draw the face.

21:07.780 --> 21:10.610
NO~

21:13.500 --> 21:15.280
The missile has been launched.

21:15.280 --> 21:17.170
Start the attack on Gouyokuou!

21:30.320 --> 21:34.710
Come on... I just want to quietly wait for her.

21:35.100 --> 21:37.610
Why won't you leave me alone?

21:38.190 --> 21:40.220
I'm Gouyokuou, King of Greed, you know.

21:40.220 --> 21:42.860
So if I simply wish for...

21:43.840 --> 21:44.780
See?

21:45.780 --> 21:50.520
Do I have to use this power in order to keep my promise?

21:55.320 --> 21:58.380
Defend us from the Water, did you say, Kyouka?

21:58.380 --> 22:01.710
Mom, where is this spaceship going?

22:02.210 --> 22:04.470
To the safest place in this universe.

23:40.570 --> 23:46.780
Kyouka. To the Midarezaki, or rather, to me, you are an irreplaceable being.

23:47.210 --> 23:52.620
Kyouka. No matter who you are or where you came from, the facts of this matter do not change.

23:52.620 --> 23:54.200
Next time: Kyouka-sama Frenzy.
